WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.699
Things are looking bright for one of Marvel
Comics' darkest characters.

00:00:03.699 --> 00:00:08.040
While critics have used their reviews to tear
Venom limb from stretchy limb, the filmgoing

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:12.169
masses appear to really be growing attached
to the symbiotic superhero movie and they've

00:00:12.169 --> 00:00:16.850
unexpectedly sent the film's audience approval
rating soaring on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:21.240
By the end of Venom's opening weekend, the
Sony Pictures production was sporting a surprisingly

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:26.699
stellar 89 percent audience approval score
on Rotten Tomatoes — a huge difference compared

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:29.160
to its much lower critical score on the site.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:33.500
The audience rating is the result of more
than 16,000 votes, seeming to indicate that

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.681
quite a few filmgoers made a point of hitting
up Rotten Tomatoes after seeing the movie

00:00:37.681 --> 00:00:39.140
to let their thoughts be known.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.289
The apparently positive audience reaction
is obviously a huge turnaround from what reviewers

00:00:43.289 --> 00:00:43.780
thought.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:48.060
When Venom slithered its slimy body onto the
silver screen at the start of October, movie

00:00:48.071 --> 00:00:51.820
critics weren't exactly loving what the symbiote
and its host had to offer.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.470
The very first reports weren't terrible, but
they seemed split on how to feel about the

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.560
not-quite-a-superhero superhero flick.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:02.280
Some found the relationship between Tom Hardy's
Eddie Brock and the alien Venom to be a highlight,

00:01:02.289 --> 00:01:05.970
while others found joy in the movie's humor,
whether it was intentional or not.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:09.680
But the inconsistent tone of the movie, along
with its failure to follow through on some

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.960
of its more interesting elements, were major
points of contention in these first impressions.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:18.420
Once Sony Pictures lifted its review embargo,
the floodgates opened, and critics took their

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:19.580
knives out on Venom.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:23.560
Some argued the movie was so bad it's good,
while others contended that the whole thing

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:24.720
was just plain bad.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.620
"Like a turd...in the wind."

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:32.960
And since its theatrical release, Venom has
sputtered to a paltry 31 percent critical

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:37.280
approval rating on Rotten Tomatoes, which
would seem to mark the Ruben Fleischer-directed

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.430
movie as a certified stinker.

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:43.960
Richard Roeper with the Chicago Sun-Times
slammed the movie as "a tone-deaf, uneven,

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:47.250
and maddeningly dumb clunker that never settles
on an identity."

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:51.969
Another critic venomously described the production
as "a chaotic, unfocused, assembly edit of

00:01:51.969 --> 00:01:56.570
a movie, that appears to have had all the
vitality and humanity parasitically sucked

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:57.120
out of it."

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:57.820
Yikes.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:01.920
Though critics and general audiences don't
always come to the same conclusion regarding

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:06.780
the quality of a film, Venom appears to be
a particularly unique case, as there's a significant

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.000
difference between the way professional reviewers
and casual moviegoers are reacting to the

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:11.500
movie.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:15.660
If you go by the numbers, from the high audience
score to the record-setting opening weekend,

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.440
it seems like audiences are straight-up loving
this movie.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:23.320
Venom is hardly the first movie that critics
and audiences have clashed over like this.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:28.280
In 2017, only 40 percent of professional reviewers
gave the Justice League movie a positive rating,

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.521
while 74 percent of the audience voters claimed
to have enjoyed it.

00:02:31.521 --> 00:02:35.870
A similar sequence of events played out in
2016 with Suicide Squad.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:39.620
The critical score for the supervillain team-up
flick came in at 28 percent.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:44.100
But once audiences saw it for themselves,
60 percent of Rotten Tomatoes voters gave

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:45.170
it a positive rating.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.260
Are the critics wrong?

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.580
Or are some audiences just that easy to please?

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:50.020
It's hard to say for certain.

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:54.170
Perhaps the most infamous recent example of
critics and fans fiercely disagreeing about

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:58.290
a movie's merits came in December 2017 with
Star Wars: The Last Jedi.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:03.540
But in that instance, the situation was flipped,
with 91 percent of reviewers loving writer-director

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.480
Rian Johnson's entry in the franchise.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:10.660
Fans of the series, however, seemed to largely
revolt against this sentiment, with only 45

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.730
percent of users saying they enjoyed it.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:15.920
So it just goes to show: this is a phenomenon
that goes both ways.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.260
Venom's opening weekend brought in over $205
million worldwide.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:24.020
Coupled with the sky-high audience score,
the people in charge at Sony will likely be

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:28.350
encouraged to press on with plans to turn
Venom into the start of a full-fledged cinematic

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:32.730
universe, using the movie as a springboard
to launch other stories from Sony's spider-focused

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.440
stable of Marvel Characters.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.650
With this kind of reception, we're almost
definitely getting a Venom 2.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:41.400
Hopefully that one can thread the needle a
little better, and serve up something critics

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.900
and audiences both love.

